<br>
</div>
<div class=3D"elementToProof" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, &quot;Aptos_Embe=
ddedFont&quot;, &quot;Aptos_MSFontService&quot;, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-s=
erif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">
I tested it before publishing. An independent system, given nothing but tha=
t URL, located a specific recording by identifier, crossed between two doma=
ins, distinguished the primary evidence from the analytical passes, and ans=
wered accurately. It also noted
 that the reading instructions I attached constrain how the material may be=
 characterized and that it would still apply its own judgment to what the e=
vidence supports. That is exactly what I built it to do.</div>
<div style=3D"direction: ltr; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em; font-fam=
